/-!
# Joint surjectivity of a representable étale family, and its ascent along a thickening

Let `S` be a scheme contained in a big fppf site `B`.

The first result here is the converse of
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.exists_index_pointsMapULift_eq`: a family `{Xₖ ⟶ X}` of
morphisms of fppf sheaves on the big fppf site of `S` which is representable by algebraic spaces
and étale, and which is jointly surjective on the points of Stacks 03BU, induces a *surjection*
of sheaves `∐ₖ Xₖ ⟶ X`. This is the family form of Stacks 05VM, of which the library carried
only the one-member case
(`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isLocallySurjective_of_isSurjective_of_flat`); the one-member
case cannot be applied to a family, because the coproduct `∐ₖ Xₖ` is not known to be
representable by algebraic spaces — that is the regular-cutoff obstruction of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoproductCutoffSharp`. No such obstruction arises here:
the covering sieve is generated by the *separate* étale charts of the base changes, never by
their coproduct, and it is reindexed by the points of the test object, which is a type in
`Type u`.

The second result is what the first was wanted for: joint surjectivity of a family of
representable étale morphisms of fppf sheaves **ascends along a representable thickening**. If
`φ : X₀ ⟶ X` is a representable thickening and a family `{Zₖ ⟶ X}` of representable étale
morphisms receives a jointly surjective family `{Yₖ ⟶ X₀}` compatibly with `φ`, then
`{Zₖ ⟶ X}` is jointly surjective. The hypothesis is only a commuting square for each `k`, not a
cartesian one, and the thickening enters only through being bijective on points
(`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.bijective_pointsMapULift_of_isRepresentableThickeningULift`): a
point of `X` comes from a point of `X₀`, that point is covered by the lower family, and its
image in `Zₖ` lies over the given point. Étaleness is needed for the upper family alone, and
only to turn joint surjectivity on points back into a surjection of sheaves.

This is the form in which local surjectivity descends along a thickening of formal algebraic
spaces: the covering form of Stacks 039R,
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.exists_affine_etale_cover_lift_of_isThickening`, crosses only a
thickening of *objects of the site*, and the base-change statements for
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective` run the other way, from the thick end to the thin
one.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_of_isRepresentableEtale`: a
  jointly surjective family of representable étale morphisms of fppf sheaves is a surjection of
  sheaves.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_of_isRepresentableThickening`:
  joint surjectivity of such a family ascends along a representable thickening of its target.

## Implementation notes

The proof of the first result follows
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isLocallySurjective_of_isSurjective_of_flat` with the single
chart replaced by one chart per index: over a scheme-valued point `ξ : T ⟶ X` of the target the
base change of each `Xₖ ⟶ X` is an algebraic space over `S`, whose étale scheme chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_etale_chart_surjective_pointsULift`) composed with the
projection is a morphism `Vₖ ⟶ T` of the site, étale because the base change is étale on every
étale chart of its source. Those morphisms are jointly surjective on the points of the scheme
underlying `T`: a point of that scheme is the underlying scheme point of a field-valued point,
the family covers its image in `X`, a compatible pair of points of a cartesian square lifts
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_pointsULift_of_isPullback`), the chart of the base change is
surjective on points, and the underlying scheme point of a field-valued point depends only on
its class (`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.schemePointULift_eq_of_class_eq`). A jointly
surjective family of flat morphisms locally of finite presentation generates a covering sieve
(`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.ofArrows_mem_topology_of_flat_lfp`), which asks for an index
type in `Type u`; the family is therefore reindexed by the points of the scheme underlying `T`,
one index being chosen for each point.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03BU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03BU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 039R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/039R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GVL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GVL)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

universe u

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### A jointly surjective representable étale family is a surjection of sheaves -/

/-- **A family of morphisms of fppf sheaves on the big fppf site of `S` which is representable
by algebraic spaces, étale, and jointly surjective on points induces a surjection of sheaves
out of the coproduct.** This is the converse of
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.exists_index_pointsMapULift_eq`, and the family form of
Stacks 05VM.

A scheme-valued point `ξ : T ⟶ X` of the target cuts out from each member an algebraic space
over `S`; an étale scheme chart of that algebraic space, followed by the projection to `T`, is a
morphism `Vₖ ⟶ T` of the site whose underlying morphism of schemes is étale, hence flat and
locally of finite presentation. These morphisms are jointly surjective on the points of the
scheme underlying `T`, so — after choosing one index per point, which brings the index type down
to `Type u` — they generate a covering sieve of `T`; and over each member of that sieve the
point `ξ` lifts into a single member of the family, through the chart. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_of_isRepresentableEtale
    {I : Type (u + 1)} {Xi : I → FppfSheaf B S hS} {X : FppfSheaf B S hS} (f : ∀ k, Xi k ⟶ X)
    (hetale : ∀ k, IsRepresentableEtale B S hS (f k))
    (hsurj : ∀ p : Space.pointsULift.{u + 1} B S hS X.obj,
      ∃ (k : I) (z : Space.pointsULift.{u + 1} B S hS (Xi k).obj),
        Space.pointsMapULift.{u + 1} B S hS (Xi k).obj (f k).hom z = p) :
    letI : HasColimitsOfSize.{u + 1, u + 1} (FppfSheaf B S hS) := Sheaf.instHasColimitsOfSize
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Sigma.desc f) := by
  let : HasColimitsOfSize.{u + 1, u + 1} (FppfSheaf B S hS) := Sheaf.instHasColimitsOfSize
  classical
  rw [Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_iff]
  intro T s
  set ξ : (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj T ⟶ X.obj := uliftYonedaEquiv.{u + 1}.symm s
  have hs : uliftYonedaEquiv.{u + 1} ξ = s := uliftYonedaEquiv.{u + 1}.apply_symm_apply s
  -- an étale scheme chart of each represented base change, surjective on points
  choose V b hbetale hbsurj using fun k ↦
    Space.exists_etale_chart_surjective_pointsULift B S hS ((hetale k).1 T ξ)
  -- the induced morphisms of the site, étale on underlying schemes
  set c : ∀ k, V k ⟶ T := fun k ↦ (ULiftYoneda.fullyFaithful (BigFppfOver B S hS)).preimage
    (b k ≫ pullback.fst ξ (f k).hom)
  have hc : ∀ k, (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map (c k) = b k ≫ pullback.fst ξ (f k).hom := fun k ↦
    (ULiftYoneda.fullyFaithful (BigFppfOver B S hS)).map_preimage _
  have hcetale : ∀ k, Etale ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (c k)) := by
    intro k
    have hrel : (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
        (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).relative (uliftYoneda.{u + 1})
        ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map (c k)) := by
      rw [hc k]
      exact (hetale k).2 T ξ (V k) (b k) (hbetale k)
    have hinv := MorphismProperty.of_relative_map hrel
    exact hinv
  -- they are jointly surjective on the points of the scheme underlying `T`
  have hpt : ∀ x : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T,
      ∃ k, x ∈ Set.range ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (c k)).base := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨K, instK, hK, ρ, hρ⟩ := Space.exists_fieldSpec_at_point B T.left.2 x
    let r : B.obj hK ⟶ T.left := B.inclusion.preimage (X := B.obj hK) (Y := T.left) ρ
    let m : (Over.mk (r ≫ T.hom) : BigFppfOver B S hS) ⟶ T := Over.homMk r
    let p : Space.FieldValuedPointULift.{u + 1} B S hS ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj T) :=
      ⟨K, hK, B.inclusion.map (r ≫ T.hom), ULift.up m⟩
    have hmρ : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map m = ρ :=
      B.inclusion.map_preimage (X := B.obj hK) (Y := T.left) ρ
    have hpx : Space.schemePointULift B S hS T p = x := by
      show (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map m (IsLocalRing.closedPoint K) = x
      rw [hmρ]
      exact hρ _
    obtain ⟨k, z, hz⟩ := hsurj (Space.pointsMapULift.{u + 1} B S hS
      ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj T) ξ (p.class B S hS _))
    obtain ⟨v, hv, -⟩ := Space.exists_pointsULift_of_isPullback B S hS
      (IsPullback.of_hasPullback ξ (f k).hom) (p.class B S hS _) z hz.symm
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hbsurj k v
    obtain ⟨w₀, rfl⟩ := Quot.exists_rep w
    have hclass : (Space.FieldValuedPointULift.map B S hS ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).obj (V k))
          ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map (c k)) w₀).class B S hS _ = p.class B S hS _ := by
      rw [← Space.pointsMapULift_class, hc k, Space.pointsMapULift_comp_apply, hw, hv]
    refine ⟨k, Space.schemePointULift B S hS (V k) w₀, ?_⟩
    show (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (c k)
      (Space.schemePointULift B S hS (V k) w₀) = x
    rw [← Space.schemePointULift_map_uliftYoneda B S hS (c k) w₀,
      schemePointULift_eq_of_class_eq' B S hS hclass, hpx]
  -- one index per point of that scheme brings the family down to an index type in `Type u`
  choose κ hκ using hpt
  refine ⟨Sieve.ofArrows (fun x ↦ V (κ x)) (fun x ↦ c (κ x)),
    ofArrows_mem_topology_of_flat_lfp' B S hS _ _ (fun x ↦ ⟨x, hκ x⟩)
      (fun x ↦ ((Etale.iff_flat_and_formallyUnramified).1 (hcetale (κ x))).1)
      (fun x ↦ ((Etale.iff_flat_and_formallyUnramified).1 (hcetale (κ x))).2.2), ?_⟩
  rintro Z g ⟨Z', e, d, ⟨x⟩, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨κ x, uliftYonedaEquiv.{u + 1}
    (((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map e ≫ b (κ x)) ≫ pullback.snd ξ (f (κ x)).hom), ?_⟩
  have hfac : (((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map e ≫ b (κ x)) ≫ pullback.snd ξ (f (κ x)).hom) ≫
      (f (κ x)).hom = (uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map (e ≫ c (κ x)) ≫ ξ := by
    rw [Category.assoc, ← pullback.condition, Functor.map_comp, hc (κ x)]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
  calc (f (κ x)).hom.app (Opposite.op Z) (uliftYonedaEquiv.{u + 1}
        (((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map e ≫ b (κ x)) ≫ pullback.snd ξ (f (κ x)).hom))
      = uliftYonedaEquiv.{u + 1} (((((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map e ≫ b (κ x)) ≫
          pullback.snd ξ (f (κ x)).hom)) ≫ (f (κ x)).hom) := (uliftYonedaEquiv_comp _ _).symm
    _ = uliftYonedaEquiv.{u + 1} ((uliftYoneda.{u + 1}).map (e ≫ c (κ x)) ≫ ξ) := by rw [hfac]
    _ = X.obj.map (e ≫ c (κ x)).op s := by
        rw [← hs]
        exact (uliftYonedaEquiv_naturality.{u + 1} ξ (e ≫ c (κ x)).op).symm

/-! ### Ascent along a representable thickening -/

/-- **Joint surjectivity of a family of representable étale morphisms of fppf sheaves ascends
along a representable thickening of the target.** Let `φ : X₀ ⟶ X` be a representable
thickening — equivalently, by Stacks 0GVL, a closed immersion inducing an isomorphism on
reductions — let `{Zₖ ⟶ X}` be a family of morphisms representable by algebraic spaces and
étale, and let `{Yₖ ⟶ X₀}` be a jointly surjective family with a morphism `Yₖ ⟶ Zₖ` over `φ`
for each `k`. Then `{Zₖ ⟶ X}` is jointly surjective.

Only a commuting square is asked of each `k`, not a cartesian one. The thickening enters
through being bijective on points: a point of `X` is the image of a point of `X₀`, which the
lower family covers, and the image of the covering point in `Zₖ` lies over the given point of
`X`. Étaleness of the upper family turns that joint surjectivity on points back into a
surjection of sheaves, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_of_isRepresentableEtale`. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_of_isRepresentableThickening
    {Xthin Xthick : FppfSheaf B S hS} (φ : Xthin ⟶ Xthick)
    (hφ : Space.IsRepresentableThickeningULift.{u + 1} B S hS φ.hom)
    {I : Type (u + 1)} {Yi Zi : I → FppfSheaf B S hS}
    (g : ∀ k, Yi k ⟶ Xthin) (f : ∀ k, Zi k ⟶ Xthick) (t : ∀ k, Yi k ⟶ Zi k)
    (hcomm : ∀ k, g k ≫ φ = t k ≫ f k)
    (hetale : ∀ k, IsRepresentableEtale B S hS (f k))
    (hcov : letI : HasColimitsOfSize.{u + 1, u + 1} (FppfSheaf B S hS) :=
        Sheaf.instHasColimitsOfSize
      Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Sigma.desc g)) :
    letI : HasColimitsOfSize.{u + 1, u + 1} (FppfSheaf B S hS) := Sheaf.instHasColimitsOfSize
    Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Sigma.desc f) := by
  let : HasColimitsOfSize.{u + 1, u + 1} (FppfSheaf B S hS) := Sheaf.instHasColimitsOfSize
  refine isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_of_isRepresentableEtale B S hS f hetale fun p ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨p₀, hp₀⟩ :=
    (bijective_pointsMapULift_of_isRepresentableThickeningULift hφ).2 p
  obtain ⟨k, z, hz⟩ := exists_index_pointsMapULift_eq B S hS g hcov p₀
  refine ⟨k, Space.pointsMapULift.{u + 1} B S hS (Yi k).obj (t k).hom z, ?_⟩
  have hhom : (t k).hom ≫ (f k).hom = (g k).hom ≫ φ.hom := congrArg (·.hom) (hcomm k).symm
  rw [← Space.pointsMapULift_comp_apply, hhom, Space.pointsMapULift_comp_apply, hz, hp₀]

end AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

end
